There are precedents in the history of NetHack. For example, people used
bells to generate an arbitrary number of nymphs (mainly useful if potions
of object detection are smoky). The DevTeam changed this so that summoned
nymphs have empty inventory. This change hardly effected the normal game
play, but playing styles which were considered abusive. But pudding
farming has been around and discussed over the course of several
versions, so it seems safe to assume that the DevTeam did not consider it
"degenerate" or see less risk of it becoming common.

